IMPORT prelude

-- Personal Data Protection Act 2012 (Singapore) -- who the data protection obligations bind and what data they reach (s 4),
-- consent and its withdrawal (ss 13 to 16), retention (s 25), data breach notification (ss 26B to 26D), the Do Not Call duties
-- (ss 43, 44, 48), the individual offences of unauthorised disclosure, improper use and re-identification (ss 48C to 48F), the
-- ceiling on financial penalties (s 48J) and the right of private action (s 48O).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PDPA2012.txt, with
-- amendments to Act 19 of 2025 (wef 5 December 2025) shown; the Act 40 of 2020 penalty ceilings are annotated wef 1 October 2022.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the duties an organisation, a
-- telemarketer or an employee actually meets, and what happens when they are broken. Not encoded: the Commission and its
-- administration (Part 2), policies and practices (s 12), purpose limitation and notification (ss 18 to 20), access and correction
-- and their Schedules (ss 21, 22, Fifth and Sixth Schedules), accuracy, protection and overseas transfer (ss 23, 24, 26), the
-- First and Second Schedule exceptions to consent (treated as a single flag), the register itself (ss 39 to 42), checkers
-- (s 43A), calling line identity (s 45), dictionary attacks (s 48B) beyond its penalty ceiling, review, directions, undertakings
-- and appeals (ss 48G to 48N, 48P to 48R), investigation powers and the s 51 offences. Part 6B (data portability) is referred to
-- throughout the deposit but its text is not in it.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Personal Data Protection Act 2012 -- obligations`

§§ `4 -- whom Parts 3 to 6A bind`

-- s 4(1): Parts 3, 4, 5, 6, 6A and 6B "do not impose any obligation on" (a) "any individual acting in a personal or domestic
-- capacity"; (b) "any employee acting in the course of his or her employment with an organisation"; (c) "any public agency".
-- s 4(2): those Parts, "except sections 24 and 25", 6A "except sections 26C(3)(a) and 26E", do not impose any obligation on a data
-- intermediary processing on behalf of another organisation "pursuant to a contract which is evidenced or made in writing".
-- s 4(3): the organisation has the same obligation for data its intermediary processes "as if the personal data were processed by
-- the organisation itself".
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `an organisation processing for its own purposes`
    `an individual acting in a personal or domestic capacity`
    `an employee acting in the course of employment`
    `a public agency`
    `a data intermediary under a written contract`
    `a data intermediary without a written contract`

DECLARE Obligation IS ONE OF
    `obtain consent (s 13)`
    `protect the data (s 24)`
    `cease to retain the data (s 25)`
    `assess a suspected breach (s 26C(2))`
    `tell the principal of a breach (s 26C(3)(a))`
    `notify the Commission of a notifiable breach (s 26D)`

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor, `the obligation` IS AN Obligation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the obligation binds the actor` IF
    CONSIDER `the actor`
    WHEN `an individual acting in a personal or domestic capacity` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an employee acting in the course of employment` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a public agency` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a data intermediary under a written contract` THEN
        CONSIDER `the obligation`
        WHEN `protect the data (s 24)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `cease to retain the data (s 25)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `tell the principal of a breach (s 26C(3)(a))` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `a data intermediary without a written contract` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the obligation`
        WHEN `tell the principal of a breach (s 26C(3)(a))` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Inference, not text: s 4(2) lifts the other duties only where the intermediary's contract is "evidenced or made in writing", so an
-- intermediary without one is read here as bound by everything, including s 26C(3)(a), which is addressed to "a data intermediary".

-- s 4(4): "This Act does not apply in respect of" (a) data "contained in a record that has been in existence for at least 100
-- years"; or (b) data about a deceased individual, "except that the provisions relating to the disclosure of personal data and
-- section 24 (protection of personal data) apply" where the individual "has been dead for 10 years or less".
GIVEN `age of the record in years` IS A NUMBER, `the individual is dead` IS A BOOLEAN, `years since death` IS A NUMBER,
      `the provision concerns disclosure or protection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the data` IF
        `age of the record in years` LESS THAN 100
    AND (    (NOT `the individual is dead`)
         OR  (`the provision concerns disclosure or protection` AND `years since death` AT MOST 10))

-- s 4(5): "Except where business contact information is expressly mentioned, Parts 3, 4, 5, 6 and 6A do not apply to business
-- contact information."
GIVEN `is business contact information` IS A BOOLEAN, `the provision expressly mentions business contact information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Parts 3 to 6A reach the information` IF
    (NOT `is business contact information`) OR `the provision expressly mentions business contact information`

§§ `13 to 16 -- consent`

-- s 13: an organisation "must not ... collect, use or disclose personal data about an individual unless" (a) the individual
-- "gives, or is deemed to have given" consent, or (b) doing so without consent "is required or authorised under this Act or any
-- other written law".
-- s 14(1): no consent unless the individual was "provided with the information required under section 20". s 14(2): an
-- organisation must not (a) require consent "beyond what is reasonable to provide the product or service", or (b) obtain consent
-- by "false or misleading information" or "deceptive or misleading practices"; (3) such consent "is not validly given".
-- s 15(1): deemed consent where the individual "voluntarily provides the personal data" for the purpose and "it is reasonable
-- that the individual would voluntarily provide the data".
-- s 15A: deemed consent by notification, from 1 February 2021, if the organisation (4)(a) assessed that the use "is not likely to
-- have an adverse effect", (b) told the individual of its intention, purpose and "a reasonable period" to object, and the
-- individual did not object in time; (3) not for "any prescribed purpose".
-- s 16(1): the individual "may at any time withdraw any consent given, or deemed to have been given"; (4) the organisation
-- "must cease ... unless" processing without consent is required or authorised.
DECLARE Processing HAS
    `date of processing` IS A NUMBER
    `consent given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `told the section 20 information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consent demanded beyond what the service needs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consent obtained by deception` IS A BOOLEAN
    `data volunteered for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable to volunteer it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `adverse-effect assessment done` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notified of intention, purpose and opt-out period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `objected within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for a prescribed purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consent withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
    `required or authorised without consent` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the processing` IS A Processing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consent is validly given` IF
        `the processing`'s `consent given`
    AND `the processing`'s `told the section 20 information`
    AND (NOT `the processing`'s `consent demanded beyond what the service needs`)
    AND (NOT `the processing`'s `consent obtained by deception`)

GIVEN `the processing` IS A Processing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consent is deemed by conduct` IF
    `the processing`'s `data volunteered for the purpose` AND `the processing`'s `reasonable to volunteer it`

GIVEN `the processing` IS A Processing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consent is deemed by notification` IF
        `the processing`'s `date of processing` AT LEAST 20210201
    AND `the processing`'s `adverse-effect assessment done`
    AND `the processing`'s `notified of intention, purpose and opt-out period`
    AND (NOT `the processing`'s `objected within the period`)
    AND (NOT `the processing`'s `for a prescribed purpose`)

GIVEN `the processing` IS A Processing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the organisation may collect, use or disclose` IF
        `the processing`'s `required or authorised without consent`
    OR  (    (NOT `the processing`'s `consent withdrawn`)
         AND (    `consent is validly given` `the processing`
              OR  `consent is deemed by conduct` `the processing`
              OR  `consent is deemed by notification` `the processing`))

§§ `25 -- retention`

-- s 25: an organisation "must cease to retain" documents containing personal data, or anonymise them, "as soon as it is
-- reasonable to assume that" (a) the purpose "is no longer being served by retention" AND (b) "retention is no longer necessary for
-- legal or business purposes".
GIVEN `the purpose is still served` IS A BOOLEAN, `needed for legal or business purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the organisation must stop retaining the data` IF
    (NOT `the purpose is still served`) AND (NOT `needed for legal or business purposes`)

§§ `26A to 26D -- data breaches`

-- s 26A: "data breach" means (a) "unauthorised access, collection, use, disclosure, copying, modification or disposal", or (b)
-- "the loss of any storage medium or device" where such things are likely.
-- s 26B(1): notifiable if it (a) "results in, or is likely to result in, significant harm to an affected individual"; or (b) "is,
-- or is likely to be, of a significant scale". (2) deemed significant harm if it involves "prescribed personal data"; (3) deemed
-- significant scale if it affects "not fewer than the prescribed number of affected individuals". (4) a breach relating to "the
-- unauthorised access, collection, use, disclosure, copying or modification of personal data only within an organisation is deemed
-- not to be a notifiable data breach". Disposal and loss of a device are not in that list.
-- The prescribed number is not in the Act; it is a parameter here.
DECLARE BreachKind IS ONE OF
    `unauthorised access`
    `unauthorised disclosure`
    `unauthorised copying`
    `unauthorised modification`
    `unauthorised disposal`
    `loss of a storage device`

DECLARE Breach HAS
    `kind` IS A BreachKind
    `only within the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `significant harm likely` IS A BOOLEAN
    `involves prescribed personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
    `significant scale likely` IS A BOOLEAN
    `individuals affected` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internal-only exclusion applies` IF
        `the breach`'s `only within the organisation`
    AND CONSIDER `the breach`'s `kind`
        WHEN `unauthorised disposal` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `loss of a storage device` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the breach is harmful in the s 26B(1)(a) sense` IF
    `the breach`'s `significant harm likely` OR `the breach`'s `involves prescribed personal data`

GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach, `the prescribed number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the breach is notifiable` IF
        (NOT `the internal-only exclusion applies` `the breach`)
    AND (    `the breach is harmful in the s 26B(1)(a) sense` `the breach`
         OR  `the breach`'s `significant scale likely`
         OR  `the breach`'s `individuals affected` AT LEAST `the prescribed number`)

-- s 26D(1): notify the Commission "as soon as is practicable, but in any case no later than 3 calendar days after the day the
-- organisation makes that assessment". Days are counted as day numbers here.
GIVEN `day of assessment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day to notify the Commission` MEANS `day of assessment` PLUS 3

-- s 26D(2): "the organisation must also notify each affected individual affected by a notifiable data breach mentioned in section
-- 26B(1)(a)" -- the harm limb only; a breach notifiable only for its scale need not be told to individuals.
-- (5) not if the organisation (a) after assessing took action "that renders it unlikely" the breach will cause significant harm, or
-- (b) had earlier implemented "any technological measure" with that effect. (6) "must not notify" if a prescribed law enforcement
-- agency "so instructs" or the Commission "so directs". (7) the Commission may waive on written application.
DECLARE Aftermath HAS
    `remedial action makes harm unlikely` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prior technological measure makes harm unlikely` IS A BOOLEAN
    `law enforcement agency instructs silence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Commission directs silence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Commission waived notification` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the aftermath` IS AN Aftermath
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notifying individuals is forbidden` IF
    `the aftermath`'s `law enforcement agency instructs silence` OR `the aftermath`'s `Commission directs silence`

GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach, `the prescribed number` IS A NUMBER, `the aftermath` IS AN Aftermath
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the organisation must notify affected individuals` IF
        `the breach is notifiable` `the breach` `the prescribed number`
    AND `the breach is harmful in the s 26B(1)(a) sense` `the breach`
    AND (NOT `the aftermath`'s `remedial action makes harm unlikely`)
    AND (NOT `the aftermath`'s `prior technological measure makes harm unlikely`)
    AND (NOT `notifying individuals is forbidden` `the aftermath`)
    AND (NOT `the aftermath`'s `Commission waived notification`)

§§ `43, 44 and 48 -- Do Not Call`

-- s 43(1): a person "must not send a specified message addressed to a Singapore telephone number unless" it has "valid
-- confirmation that the Singapore telephone number is not listed in the relevant register". (2) valid confirmation is (a) the
-- Commission's confirmation "within the prescribed duration before sending", or (b) a checker's information where the person "has
-- no reason to believe that, and is not reckless as to whether" the prescribed period has expired or the information is false.
-- (4) no contravention if the subscriber or user "gave clear and unambiguous consent" that is "evidenced in written or other form".
-- s 48(2): s 43(1) and s 44 do not apply to an employee who sends "in good faith" in the course of employment or on the employer's
-- instructions; (4) except an officer or partner who "knew or ought reasonably to have known" the number was listed and the message
-- was sent "with Z's consent or connivance" or through "neglect on Z's part".
DECLARE Message HAS
    `Commission confirmation within the prescribed duration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `checker says not listed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reason to suspect the checker information is stale or false` IS A BOOLEAN
    `clear consent evidenced in accessible form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sent by an employee in good faith for the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sender is an officer or partner who knew and consented or neglected` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the message` IS A Message
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sender has valid confirmation` IF
        `the message`'s `Commission confirmation within the prescribed duration`
    OR  (`the message`'s `checker says not listed` AND (NOT `the message`'s `reason to suspect the checker information is stale or false`))

GIVEN `the message` IS A Message
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee exemption applies` IF
    `the message`'s `sent by an employee in good faith for the employer`
    AND (NOT `the message`'s `sender is an officer or partner who knew and consented or neglected`)

GIVEN `the message` IS A Message
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sending the message contravenes s 43` IF
        (NOT `the sender has valid confirmation` `the message`)
    AND (NOT `the message`'s `clear consent evidenced in accessible form`)
    AND (NOT `the employee exemption applies` `the message`)

-- s 44: the message must identify the sender, say how to contact it, and (d) that information must be "reasonably likely to be
-- valid for at least 30 days after the message is sent".
GIVEN `identifies the sender` IS A BOOLEAN, `says how to contact the sender` IS A BOOLEAN, `days the details stay valid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contact information complies with s 44` IF
    `identifies the sender` AND `says how to contact the sender` AND `days the details stay valid` AT LEAST 30

§§ `48C to 48F -- offences by individuals`

-- s 48D(1): an individual who discloses personal data held by an organisation or public agency, where the disclosure "is not
-- authorised", "knowing" that or "reckless as to whether" it is authorised, is guilty of an offence: "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or
-- ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or ... both". s 48E(1): the same for use, but only if the individual as a result
-- "obtains a gain", "causes harm to another individual" or "causes a loss to another person". s 48F(1): the same for re-identifying
-- anonymised information. Defences (ss 48D(2), 48E(2), 48F(2)), to be proved "on a balance of probabilities", include public
-- availability, other law, court order, and (48D, 48E) a reasonable belief in a legal right. s 48C(2): the Part does not apply to a
-- "relevant public official in a Singapore public sector agency".
DECLARE Misuse IS ONE OF
    `disclosure (s 48D)`
    `use (s 48E)`
    `re-identification (s 48F)`

DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `what was done` IS A Misuse
    `authorised by the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or was reckless that it was unauthorised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resulted in gain, harm or loss` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a defence is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a relevant public official` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual commits an offence under Part 9B` IF
        (NOT `the conduct`'s `authorised by the organisation`)
    AND `the conduct`'s `knew or was reckless that it was unauthorised`
    AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `a defence is proved`)
    AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `a relevant public official`)
    AND CONSIDER `the conduct`'s `what was done`
        WHEN `use (s 48E)` THEN `the conduct`'s `resulted in gain, harm or loss`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the misuse` IS A Misuse
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for the misuse` MEANS 5000

GIVEN `the misuse` IS A Misuse
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years for the misuse` MEANS 2

§§ `48J -- financial penalties`

-- s 48J(1): the Commission may impose a financial penalty if satisfied an organisation "intentionally or negligently contravened"
-- Parts 3 to 6B, or a person Part 9 or s 48B(1). (2) not for a contravention "the breach of which is an offence under this Act".
-- (3) organisations, Parts 3 to 6B: (a) for a contravention after the commencement of s 24 of the 2020 amendment Act by an
-- organisation "whose annual turnover in Singapore exceeds $10 million -- 10% of the annual turnover in Singapore"; (b) "in any
-- other case -- $1 million". (4) Part 9: (a) an individual $200,000; (b) any other case $1 million. (4A) s 48B(1): (a) an individual
-- $200,000; (b) after that commencement, turnover in Singapore exceeding $20 million, 5% of it; (c) otherwise $1 million. These are
-- ceilings on the prescribed maximum ("in no case may be more than"), not the penalty.
-- The commencement date is not printed in the section; 20221001 is read from the annotation "[Act 40 of 2020 wef 01/10/2022]"
-- under s 48J(3), an inference.
DECLARE Contravention IS ONE OF
    `Parts 3 to 6B by an organisation`
    `Part 9 Do Not Call`
    `s 48B dictionary attack`

GIVEN `intentional or negligent` IS A BOOLEAN, `the breach is itself an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a financial penalty may be imposed` IF
    `intentional or negligent` AND (NOT `the breach is itself an offence`)

GIVEN `the contravention` IS A Contravention, `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `annual turnover in Singapore` IS A NUMBER,
      `date of contravention` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ceiling on the financial penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the contravention`
    WHEN `Parts 3 to 6B by an organisation` THEN
        IF `date of contravention` AT LEAST 20221001 AND `annual turnover in Singapore` GREATER THAN 10000000
        THEN `annual turnover in Singapore` TIMES 0.1
        ELSE 1000000
    WHEN `Part 9 Do Not Call` THEN
        IF `is an individual` THEN 200000 ELSE 1000000
    WHEN `s 48B dictionary attack` THEN
        IF `is an individual` THEN 200000
        ELSE `the s 48B ceiling for others` `annual turnover in Singapore` `date of contravention`

GIVEN `turnover` IS A NUMBER, `on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 48B ceiling for others` MEANS
    IF `on` AT LEAST 20221001 AND `turnover` GREATER THAN 20000000
    THEN `turnover` TIMES 0.05
    ELSE 1000000

§§ `48O -- right of private action`

-- s 48O(1): "A person who suffers loss or damage directly as a result of a contravention" by an organisation "of any provision of
-- Part 4, 5, 6, 6A or 6B", or by a person of "Division 3 of Part 9 or section 48B(1)", "has a right of action for relief in civil
-- proceedings". Part 3 (compliance, policies and practices) is not in the list. (2) where the Commission has made a decision, the
-- action "may not be brought ... until after the decision has become final".
DECLARE Provision IS ONE OF
    `Part 3 policies and practices`
    `Part 4 consent and purpose`
    `Part 5 access and correction`
    `Part 6 care of personal data`
    `Part 6A breach notification`
    `Part 9 Division 3 Do Not Call`
    `s 48B dictionary attacks`

GIVEN `the provision` IS A Provision, `loss suffered directly` IS A BOOLEAN, `a Commission decision is still open to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a private action may be brought now` IF
        `loss suffered directly`
    AND (NOT `a Commission decision is still open to appeal`)
    AND CONSIDER `the provision`
        WHEN `Part 3 policies and practices` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
